    "durationMs": 281497,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Summary of what was built:\n\n**Implementation** — ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API with EF Core 8 + Npgsql:\n- `POST /links` — validates url (absolute http/https with host) and code (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), returns 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the submitted URL unchanged, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code. Codes are generated as 8 random chars, with unique-index race handling via `PostgresException 23505` retry.\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with code/url/clicks, 404 unknown.\n- `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with `Location` set to the stored URL; clicks incremented atomically with `ExecuteUpdateAsync` (verified: 10 parallel requests → exactly +10).\n- `GET /links` — `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order.\n\n**Persistence** — `Links` table with a unique `Code` index, created by an EF Core migration; `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL) is parsed into an Npgsql connection string at startup, creating the database if it doesn't exist.\n\n**Startup** — `sh start.sh` builds if the binary is missing, runs the app once with `--apply-migrations` to apply pending migrations, then `exec`s the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (confirmed by Kestrel's log and by hitting the container IP). The README documents how to start it.\n\n**Verified end-to-end** — all 22 HTTP test cases passed, and a full server restart confirmed links and click counts persist. The test server has been stopped."
